// A1.1 course art manifest — Wave 2, 2026-09-19.
//
// Today every entry renders through code: `characters[name]` and
// `situations[id]` name their component (`CharacterAvatar` / `SituationScene`,
// src/components/illustrations/) and carry `src`/`srcSmall: null`, so the
// components (see their own headers) take the inline-SVG branch. This is
// deliberately not "unfinished" — `generatedWith.status: 'svg-inline'` says the
// art IS this, today, on purpose: docs/design/a11-art-style.md's BLOCKED note
// explains why the AI-generated bytes from the earlier Higgsfield run could
// not be downloaded into this sandbox.
//
// SWAPPING IN THE OWNER'S PHOTOS. When the paste-ready prompt in
// docs/owner-prompts.md ("Generate the A1.1 course art") is run locally, it
// produces WebP files under `public/art/a11/`. Filling this manifest with
// their paths is the entire integration: set `src` (and `srcSmall` for a
// situation) to the public path, e.g.
//   characters.Ana.src = '/art/a11/char-ana-512.webp'
//   situations['a1.1-l01'].src = '/art/a11/scene-l01-1280.webp'
//   situations['a1.1-l01'].srcSmall = '/art/a11/scene-l01-640.webp'
// Nothing else changes: `CharacterAvatar` and `SituationScene` already branch
// on `src`/`srcSmall` and render `<img loading="lazy" width height alt>`
// instead of the SVG the moment a path appears here. Bump `generatedWith` to
// record the real run once any entry is filled — do not leave `svg-inline` on
// a manifest that ships a mix of photos and placeholders.
//
// `alt` here is what ships to a learner (via `role="img"` on the SVG branch,
// `alt` on the `<img>` branch); `tests/course-art.test.mjs` requires every
// entry to have a non-empty one and pins that every Lektion id and every
// A11_META.characters[].name resolves here.

